{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1011390-essence-and-magical-style","id":1011390,"title":"Essence and magical style.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-02T23:30:48-08:00","id":1011390,"title":"Essence and magical style.","content":"I'd like to expand on this because right now I only have one idea for each one, at least that could have clear gameplay effects.<br /> <br /> Pattern: It's easier for you to learn and make rotes.<br /> <br /> Dynamic: It's easier for you to get away with really off-the-wall freeform magic.<br /> <br /> Primordial: It's easier for you to avoid Paradox, because your magic tends to adhere to mythic threads.<br /> <br /> Questing: You can use Quintessence of any Resonance without penalty, and get bonuses if you use a balanced mix of Quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T03:29:05-08:00","id":1011440,"title":"","content":"Widderslainte Essences. I thought a positive and a negative would be appropriate, to represent how skewed they are.<br /> <br /> Destruction: It's easier to inflict damage and unmake - an automatic success is given. Conjuration, healing and fortifying is harder - an additional success is needed.<br /> In the case of spells like conjuring a fireball, the positive and negative cancel each other out.<br /> &quot;<i>Destruction Essences are devoted to releasing the energy in all things. Static patterns are merely fireballs and explosions waiting to happen.</i> <i>Destruction Essence pushes the Widderslainte inevitably to tear down order, to smash patterns and to tumble structures.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Frozen: Max 1 Paradox for coincidental botches. (instead of 1 per dot in highest Sphere) Vulgar with witnesses successes give 3 Paradox (instead of 1), and vulgar with witnesses botches give 4 + 3 per dot of highest Sphere (instead of 2 + 2 per dot of highest Sphere). Vulgar without witnesses failures give two points of Paradox (instead of none).<br /> (Subtlety and a clinical approach to Magick.)<br /> &quot;<i>They abhor wildness in all its forms, and devote themselves to reining in and breaking that sort of dynamic chaos. (...) Their magical styles are subtle and swift, and they rarely invest in visible effects when they can avoid it.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Chaotic: Vulgar successes - with or without witnesses - give no Paradox (instead of 1), and vulgar botches give 1 Paradox + 1 per highest Sphere dot regardless of witnesses. Coincidental spells require two additional successes.<br /> (More effective when fraying at the Tapestry.)<br /> &quot;<i>A Chaotic Essence has no interest in anything remaining the way it is. If it's broken, the mission is to repair it \u2014 just in time to smash it to flinders. All systems are bad and need to be destroyed, all order must be subverted, and wherever there are two bricks on top of one another, they need to be knocked down.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Tormented: Quintessence spent for outlandish and godlike feats (10-20 and 20+ successes required) counts double, and the difficulty can be reduced by a maximum of -6. Coincidental failures give two points of Paradox. (instead of none)<br /> (To explain the wanderlust and inability to find a place for themselves - they are constantly driven to achieve something beyond the current reality.)<br /> &quot;<i> (...) They just know that they are driven to go from place to place, bringing ruin wherever they go. These are the dreamers, if they can be called such, of the Widderslainte, the ones who quest after something greater than the destruction they can cause on their own. Fortunately, they don't always find it.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Edit:</b></u><br /> In group castings, only the given Widderslainte gets their Essence's Paradox reduction or increase.<br /> Destructive ones adjust successes needed for the whole group.<br /> Chaotics suffer +2 difficulty just for themselves in coincidental group castings; unless only Chaotics are involved - then two additional successes are needed instead.<br /> In a group casting, only the Tormented ones benefit from the Quintessence spent counting double.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Edit 2:</b></u><br /> Added quotes from <i>the </i><i><i>B</i>ook of Madness</i> 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 02-15-2017, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}